=== meta ===
rule: TEST_DISABLED
issue: 419
title: a collect_ignore guarded by `except Exception` is no compat gate, and an opaque edit beside it no longer holds it at warn
origin: #419 implementation stop and ruling of 2026-10-16 (issuecomment-6209672882, issuecomment-6209791221):
origin2: the literal effect of Q1 (b) (issuecomment-6170353038). Only the import gate, a `try` body of
origin3: plain imports (`import X` or `from X import ...`) under `except ImportError` or
origin4: `except ModuleNotFoundError`, is recorded as the condition `find_spec("X") is None`
origin5: (frontend _handler_guard / _IMPORT_ERRORS; collect_ignore_import_gate_neg). Any other except
origin6: guard is recorded as the exception text, which is no condition: guard_can_be_false still
origin7: counts it, so this is not an unguarded suite control, and compat_gate_for grants nothing. Until
origin8: #419 the opaque scripts/deploy.sh held it at warn (REPAIR_EVIDENCE); a Python conftest now
origin9: refuses that evidence for TEST_DISABLED, so it blocks and names the opaque change.
